1
00:04:45,714 --> 00:04:51,714
Some urban legends are real.

2
00:09:31,428 --> 00:09:37,428
The Shortcut is a mystery, horror, thriller film directed by Nicholaus Goossen.

3
00:14:17,142 --> 00:14:23,142
When Derek moves to a new town and discovers a shortcut through the woods to his high school, he learns about a
crazy old man who lives near its path: Legend has it that he abducted a group of teenagers years ago.

4
00:19:02,857 --> 00:19:08,857
Ignoring the warning, Derek and his friends set out to uncover
the dark secret that's buried deep in the woods.

5
00:23:48,571 --> 00:23:54,571
But will they survive to tell it?

6
00:28:34,285 --> 00:28:40,285
Derek, played by Drew Seeley.

7
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Lisa, played by Shannon Woodward.

8
00:38:05,714 --> 00:38:11,714
Mark, played by Dave Franco.

9
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Christy, played by Katrina Bowden.

10
00:47:37,142 --> 00:47:43,142
Old Man / Ivor, played by Raymond J. Barry.

11
00:52:22,857 --> 00:52:28,857
Mr. Hartley, played by Kent Allen.

12
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
The Shortcut is a 2009 American horror film directed by Nicholaus Goossen.

13
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
The film stars Andrew Seeley, Shannon Woodward, Dave Franco, and Katrina Bowden.

14
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The plot centers on two brothers who discover a rarely
used shortcut and learn its dark secret.

15
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Dan Hannon and Scott Sandler developed the screenplay in 2008 for Scary Madison Productions, the newly formed horror division of Happy Madison
Productions, the production company of Sandler's brother Adam, and Leomax Entertainment, who financed and co-produced the film.

16
01:16:11,428 --> 01:16:17,428
Released in North America by Indigomotion, a division of Leomax, on September 29,
2009, the film received mixed reviews and was a commercial failure.

17
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
It ended up being the only film under the Scary Madison label, as
it was retired in response to the film's failure.

18
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
The film was released on DVD and Blu-Ray in North
America by Anchor Bay Entertainment.

19
01:30:28,571 --> 01:30:34,571
The film explores themes of high school, woods, urban legend.

20
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
The tone is intense and dark and thought_provoking.
